,"messageType":"Alert","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Likely","urgency":"Expected","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Aberdeen SD","headline":"Flood Warning issued July 31 at 9:10AM CDT until August 1 at 2:00PM CDT by NWS Aberdeen SD","description":"...The National Weather Service in Aberdeen has issued a Flood\nWarning for the following rivers in South Dakota...\n\nLittle Minnesota River near Peever affecting Roberts County.\n\n.For sites with a river forecast, the forecast includes precipitation\nthrough the next 24 hours. Any future precipitation could affect the\nforecasts.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Little Minnesota River near Peever.\n\n* WHEN...Until Saturday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 17.0 feet, Left bank below gage begins flooding.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 8:00 AM CDT Friday the stage was 16.9 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise above flood stage late\nthis morning to a crest of 17.2 feet this afternoon. It will then\nfall below flood stage by early this evening.\n- Flood stage is 17.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nMotorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov/abr.\n\nThe next statement will be issued this evening at 830 PM CDT.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLWABR"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS43 KABR 311410"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING IN EFFECT UNTIL SATURDAY AFTERNOON"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.NEW.KABR.FL.W.0007.260731T1433Z-260801T1900Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-01T14:00:00-05:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["FLW"],"NationalWeatherService":["FLW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.edb887d76685eea2c2eba135a309286fabacf932.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-83.13,29.32],[-83.17,29.29],[-83.49,29.18],[-83.57,29.25],[-83.66,29.38],[-83.65,29.47],[-83.57,29.6],[-83.36,29.69],[-83.34,29.53],[-83.16,29.45],[-83.13,29.4],[-83.13,29.32]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.edb887d76685eea2c2eba135a309286fabacf932.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.edb887d76685eea2c2eba135a309286fabacf932.001.1","areaDesc":"Coastal waters from  Suwannee River to Keaton Beach out 20 NM; Waters from Suwannee River to Apalachicola FL from 20 to 60 NM","geocode":{"SAME":["077765","077775"],"UGC":["GMZ765","GMZ775"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/forecast/GMZ765","https://api.weather.gov/zones/forecast/GMZ775"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1e5e3381cdc977101e1a035fd97fa3fcbde276e2.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1e5e3381cdc977101e1a035fd97fa3fcbde276e2.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-07-31T11:43:00-04:00"}],"sent":"2026-07-31T12:38:00-04:00","effective":"2026-07-31T12:38:00-04:00","onset":"2026-07-31T12:38:00-04:00","expires":"2026-07-31T13:15:00-04:00","ends":"2026-07-31T13:15:00-04:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Likely","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Special Marine Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Tallahassee FL","headline":"Special Marine Warning issued July 31 at 12:38PM EDT until July 31 at 1:15PM EDT by NWS Tallahassee FL","description":"For the following areas...\nCoastal waters from  Suwannee River to Keaton Beach out 20 NM...\nWaters from Suwannee River to Apalachicola FL from 20 to 60 NM...\n\nAt 1238 PM EDT, severe thunderstorms capable of producing waterspouts\nwere located along a line extending from 13 nm north of Suwannee\nRiver to 27 nm southwest of Cedar Key, moving southeast at 20 knots.\n\nHAZARD...Waterspouts, wind gusts 34 knots or greater, and small\nhail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Waterspouts can quickly form and capsize boats...damage\nvessels...and create suddenly higher waves. Make sure all\non board are in a secure location and wearing life jackets.\nExpect wind gusts in excess of 34 knots...suddenly higher\nwaves...frequent lightning...and heavy downpours. Make sure\nall on board are wearing life jackets.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nHorseshoe Beach and Suwannee River.","instruction":"Move to safe harbor until hazardous weather passes.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["MWSTAE"],"WMOidentifier":["FZUS72 KTAE 311638"],"NWSheadline":["A SPECIAL MARINE WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL 115 PM EDT"],"eventMotionDescription":["2026-07-31T16:38:00-00:00...storm...304DEG...19KT...29.52,-83.13 28.95,-83.51"],"waterspoutDetection":["POSSIBLE"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KTAE.MA.W.0266.000000T0000Z-260731T1715Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-07-31T13:15:00-04:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["NWS"],"NationalWeatherService":["MAW"]}}}]}